{"name":"Cranbrook","hex":"#a65570","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cranbrook","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A place in England:\nA new town and civil parish with a town council in East Devon district, Devon . \n\nA small town in Cranbrook and Sissinghurst parish, Tunbridge Wells borough, Kent .\nA suburb of Ilford, borough of Redbridge, Greater London .","A new town and civil parish with a town council in East Devon district, Devon ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cranbrook"}],"entries":[{"title":"Earl of Cranbrook","blocks":[{"text":"Earl of Cranbrook, in the County of Kent, is a title in the Peerage of the United Kingdom. It was created in 1892 for the Conservative politician Gathorne Gathorne-Hardy, Viscount Cranbrook. The family seat was Hemsted Park, near Benenden, Kent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Coronet_of_a_British_Earl.svg/330px-Coronet_of_a_British_Earl.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earl_of_Cranbrook"},{"title":"Gathorne Gathorne-Hardy, 1st Earl of Cranbrook","blocks":[{"text":"Gathorne Gathorne-Hardy, 1st Earl of Cranbrook, was a prominent British Conservative politician. He held cabinet office in every Conservative government between 1858 and 1892."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/1st_Earl_of_Cranbrook.jpg/330px-1st_Earl_of_Cranbrook.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gathorne_Gathorne-Hardy%2C_1st_Earl_of_Cranbrook"},{"title":"Cranbrook (ward)","blocks":[{"text":"Cranbrook is an electoral ward in the London Borough of Redbridge. The ward has existed since the creation of the borough on 1 April 1965 and was first used in the 1964 elections. It returns councillors to Redbridge London Borough Council."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cranbrook_(ward)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Gathorne_Gathorne-Hardy%2C_Vanity_Fair%2C_1872-04-20.jpg/500px-Gathorne_Gathorne-Hardy%2C_Vanity_Fair%2C_1872-04-20.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Gathorne_Gathorne-Hardy%2C_Vanity_Fair%2C_1872-04-20.jpg/1280px-Gathorne_Gathorne-Hardy%2C_Vanity_Fair%2C_1872-04-20.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Gathorne_Gathorne-Hardy%2C_Vanity_Fair%2C_1872-04-20.jpg/500px-Gathorne_Gathorne-Hardy%2C_Vanity_Fair%2C_1872-04-20.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Conservative\". Caricature by Adriano Cecioni published in Vanity Fair in 1872","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGathorne_Gathorne-Hardy%2C_Vanity_Fair%2C_1872-04-20.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/The_Derby_Cabinet_of_1867.jpg/500px-The_Derby_Cabinet_of_1867.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/The_Derby_Cabinet_of_1867.jpg/500px-The_Derby_Cabinet_of_1867.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Derby cabinet of 1867.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Derby_Cabinet_of_1867.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Gathorne_Gathorne-Hardy_by_George_Richmond.jpg/500px-Gathorne_Gathorne-Hardy_by_George_Richmond.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Gathorne_Gathorne-Hardy_by_George_Richmond.jpg/500px-Gathorne_Gathorne-Hardy_by_George_Richmond.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Portrait of Gathor